"""Fixed app-help text for Help mode. Written from docs/UserGuide.md; keep the two in step and claim only what works."""

HELP_TEXT = """\
learnSWE app help. This is help about the app itself, not course material.
- Overview: your lessons completed, practice average and topics to revise, read from the server. "View full progress" opens the Progress page, which lists lesson progress per course, your best and latest practice scores and topics to revise.
- Study materials: the lessons your teachers have published in your courses. Choose a course, filter by topic, search by title and open a lesson. You can mark a lesson complete or incomplete; this is saved on the server and kept after you sign out.
- Practice: the Practice page lists the practice sets your teachers published in your courses. Open a set, answer every question, then submit the whole set in one step. If a question is unanswered nothing is sent and the page lists the missing question numbers. After a successful submission the page shows your score and, for each question, your choice, the correct answer and an explanation, and the choices lock. "Start another attempt" gives an empty form. If the server cannot be reached the page says so, keeps your answers and offers "Try again".
- Inbox: your targeted feedback requests, with drafts saved privately so you can resume them, and Messages from administrators. Opening a message marks it read.
- Study companion: the chat icon at the bottom right of every student page. Escape or the minimise button hides it and keeps your chat and unsent text. The refresh icon clears the chat. Reloading the browser clears it too.
- Companion limits: each message can be up to 1,000 characters, and you can send up to 20 messages a minute and 300 a day. Limits are per signed-in student account.
- Before you submit a practice set the companion gives hints and guiding questions only; it does not give or confirm answers. After you submit, it can explain that attempt.
- Teacher materials library supports real private PDF/text uploads and topic organisation. Originals persist in PostgreSQL across restarts, with10 MiB per file and100 MiB total upload storage; uploads do not publish lessons. Teacher AI content studio generates and saves unpublished draft notes from an authorised source. Teachers can edit and explicitly save notes. In Practice questions, generate three MCQs from one authorised source and reopen saved batches, including choices, correct answers and explanations. AI output requires review; teachers can edit all three questions together; teachers can publish reviewed notes or one complete three-question batch once, with a required title and course topic. Notes appear in student Study materials after refresh. Published content lists immutable snapshots. Some admin screens, such as Analytics and Feedback insights, still show sample data.
- Teacher draft editing: open a saved draft in AI content studio, choose Edit notes, then Save changes or Cancel. Unsaved changes prompt before in-app navigation. Conflicts offer loading the latest saved version; editing never calls AI or publishes notes. Teacher data requires sign-in and course membership. Teachers can permanently delete unpublished notes or whole MCQ batches after confirmation, and delete source materials only when no drafts reference them. Published snapshots prevent deleting their originating drafts. Later draft edits cannot update or republish the snapshot. Publication does not call AI.
"""
